</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Reasons for expanding the context window of models from Qwen2.5-Math series.</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Initially, we uses the setting of Section <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Performance of Intra-group and Inter-group Advantages. ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Conditional Advantage Estimation for Reinforcement Learning in Large Rea-soning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>; however, during the training process, too much length clipping (&gt; 30%) results in nearly incomparable experimental outcomes, as shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ C.3 Reasons for expanding the context window of models from Qwen2.5-Math series. ‣ Appendix C Experiments Details. ‣ Conditional Advantage Estimation for Reinforcement Learning in Large Rea-soning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. Therefore, we expand Qwen2.5-Math-7B’s context limit from 4096 to 16384 and set the maximum output length to 8192, which alleviates this phenomenon.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F9" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F9.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:131.2pt;"><img src="2509.23962v1/length_clip.png" id="A3.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:163/98;" width="163" height="98" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>The ratio of answers truncated due to reaching the maximum output length.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F9.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:254.4pt;"><img src="2509.23962v1/new_data.png" id="A3.F9.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:316/101;" width="316" height="101" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>The score curves of the training set and validation set from the newly constructed dataset with 35k data and the original dataset used for the Qwen series models, respectively.</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>System prompt.</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the training and inference of Qwen series models, we share the same system prompt as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="204.73" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 204.73" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,204.73) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 1.38 L 0 203.35 C 0 204.11 0.62 204.73 1.38 204.73 L 548.62 204.73 C 549.38 204.73 550 204.11 550 203.35 L 550 1.38 C 550 0.62 549.38 0 548.62 0 L 1.38 0 C 0.62 0 0 0.62 0 1.38 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F0F0FF;" fill="#F0F0FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 1.38 L 1.38 203.35 L 548.62 203.35 L 548.62 1.38 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.07 15.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.7em;--ltx-fo-height:12.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="178.35" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 175.66)" width="507.82"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.7em;">
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Your task is to follow a systematic, thorough reasoning process before providing the final solution. This involves analyzing, summarizing, exploring, reassessing, and refining your thought process through multiple iterations. Structure your response into two sections: Thought and Solution. In the Thought section, present your reasoning using the format: “<code id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;think&gt;\n</code> thoughts <code id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/think&gt;\n</code>”. Each thought should include detailed analysis, brainstorming, verification, and refinement of ideas. After “<code id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/think&gt;\n</code>” in the Solution section, provide the final, logical, and accurate answer, clearly derived from the exploration in the Thought section. If applicable, include the answer in <code id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">\boxed{}</code> for closed-form results like multiple choices or mathematical solutions.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>Construction of training dataset for Llama3.1-8B.</h3>

<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since the pretraining of Llama3.1-8B lacks data for long chain-of-thought and mathematical reasoning, its average training reward based on the original dataset used for Qwen2.5-Math remains below 0.2. To enhance training efficiency, we employ three Llama series models (Llama3.1-8B, Llama3.1-8B-Instruct, and Llama3.1-70B) to generate solutions for each problem across four datasets (training set of GSM8k <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, training set of MATH <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, a 46k subset of OpenR1-Math-220k <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yan et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, and DeepMath-103k <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2025</a>)</cite>). We then filter out questions whose accuracy of <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Pass@8}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Pass@8</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Pass@8}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, ultimately selecting 35k samples for training the Llama3.1-8B model. Concurrently, due to Llama3.1-8B’s limited instruction-following capability, we simplify the output format requirements in its system prompt.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS5.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="171.52" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 171.52" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,171.52) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 1.38 L 0 170.14 C 0 170.9 0.62 171.52 1.38 171.52 L 548.62 171.52 C 549.38 171.52 550 170.9 550 170.14 L 550 1.38 C 550 0.62 549.38 0 548.62 0 L 1.38 0 C 0.62 0 0 0.62 0 1.38 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F0F0FF;" fill="#F0F0FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 1.38 L 1.38 170.14 L 548.62 170.14 L 548.62 1.38 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.07 15.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.7em;--ltx-fo-height:10.29em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="145.14" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 142.45)" width="507.82"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS5.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.7em;">
<span id="A3.SS5.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Your task is to follow a systematic, thorough reasoning process before providing the final solution. This involves analyzing, summarizing, exploring, reassessing, and refining your thought process through multiple iterations. Structure your response into two sections: Thought and Solution. In the Thought section, each thought should include detailed analysis, brainstorming, verification, and refinement of ideas. In the Solution section, provide the final, logical, and accurate answer, clearly derived from the exploration in the Thought section. If applicable, include the answer in <code id="A3.SS5.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">\boxed{}</code> for closed-form results like multiple choices or mathematical solutions. Let’s think step by step.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The training curves for this 35k dataset and the original 46k training dataset over 150 training steps are shown in the Figure <a href="#A3.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ C.3 Reasons for expanding the context window of models from Qwen2.5-Math series. ‣ Appendix C Experiments Details. ‣ Conditional Advantage Estimation for Reinforcement Learning in Large Rea-soning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. It demonstrates that Llama3.1-8B has significantly higher learning effectiveness on the newly constructed dataset.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.6 </span>Scheduling strategies of coefficient to balance <span id="A3.SS6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CANON-Inter</span> and <span id="A3.SS6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CANON-Intra</span>.</h3>

<div id="A3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We try four different scheduling strategies and show the best of them for each model. Figure <a href="#A3.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ C.6 Scheduling strategies of coefficient to balance CANON-Inter and CANON-Intra. ‣ Appendix C Experiments Details. ‣ Conditional Advantage Estimation for Reinforcement Learning in Large Rea-soning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> shows the dynamics of <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> in the training process from the <span id="A3.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">First-Inter-Later-Intra</span> (<math id="A3.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=1-\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=1-\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) and <span id="A3.SS6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">First-Intra-Later-Inter</span> (<math id="A3.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>). <span id="A3.SS6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Cosin-First-Inter-Later-Intra</span> and <span id="A3.SS6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Cosin-First-Intra-Later-Inter</span> schedule the value of <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> with a cosine annealing function <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> with restarts and warm-up:</p>
<table id="A3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi=\begin{cases}\mu_{\max}\cdot\dfrac{s+1}{w}&amp;\text{if }s&lt;w\\[10.0pt]
\mu_{\min}+\dfrac{1}{2}(\mu_{\max}-\mu_{\min})\left(1+\cos\left(\pi\cdot\dfrac{s^{\prime}}{\left\lfloor\frac{S-w}{c}\right\rfloor}\right)\right)&amp;\text{if }s\geq w\text{ and }s^{\prime}=s-w\text{ mod }\left\lfloor\frac{S-w}{c}\right\rfloor\end{cases}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>w</mi></mfrac></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> mod </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi=\begin{cases}\mu_{\max}\cdot\dfrac{s+1}{w}&amp;\text{if }s&lt;w\\[10.0pt]
\mu_{\min}+\dfrac{1}{2}(\mu_{\max}-\mu_{\min})\left(1+\cos\left(\pi\cdot\dfrac{s^{\prime}}{\left\lfloor\frac{S-w}{c}\right\rfloor}\right)\right)&amp;\text{if }s\geq w\text{ and }s^{\prime}=s-w\text{ mod }\left\lfloor\frac{S-w}{c}\right\rfloor\end{cases},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of restart and <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is the warm-up step. <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is the current step of training and <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is the total step. <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the specified maximum and minimum values of <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. We use <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=30</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=150" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=150</annotation></semantics></math> for both strategies.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In strategy <span id="A3.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Cosin-First-Inter-Later-Intra</span>, we utilize <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\max}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\max}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\min}=0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\min}=0.4</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, while in strategy <span id="A3.SS6.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Cosin-First-Intra-Later-Inter</span>, we utilize <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=1-\Psi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=1-\Psi)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\max}=0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\max}=0.6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\min}=0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\min}=0.0</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. The changes in <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> under these strategies are shown in the Figure <a href="#A3.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ C.6 Scheduling strategies of coefficient to balance CANON-Inter and CANON-Intra. ‣ Appendix C Experiments Details. ‣ Conditional Advantage Estimation for Reinforcement Learning in Large Rea-soning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>. Ultimately, based on training performance, we selected strategy <span id="A3.SS6.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Cosin-First-Inter-Later-Intra</span> for Qwen2.5-7B and Llama, and strategy <span id="A3.SS6.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">First-Inter-Later-Intra</span> for Qwen2.5-1.5B.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F11" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F11.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:170.9pt;"><img src="2509.23962v1/sch1.png" id="A3.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:213/131;" width="213" height="131" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>The changes of <math id="A3.F11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> for two scheduling strategies based on accuracy during training.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F11.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:210.7pt;"><img src="2509.23962v1/sch2.png" id="A3.F11.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:262/135;" width="262" height="135" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>The changes of <math id="A3.F11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> for two scheduling strategies based on training steps during training.</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Detailed derivation of Theorem <a href="#S4.EGx6" title="Theorem 1 (Situations with clearer advantage signal (proved in Appendix )). ‣ 4.2 Advantage Estimation Based On Regrouping. ‣ 4 Conditional Advantage Estimation ‣ Conditional Advantage Estimation for Reinforcement Learning in Large Rea-soning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="Thmtheorem1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Situations with clearer advantage signal)<span id="Thmtheorem1a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that condition c is based on numerical comparisons and can be derived through sorting of metrics. Further assume that the sampled response <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> to query <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy condition c with probability <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}_{o\text{~satisfy~}c}[R_{o}]\neq\mathbf{E}_{o\text{~not ~satisfy~}c}[R_{o}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> satisfy </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> not  satisfy </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}_{o\text{~satisfy~}c}[R_{o}]\neq\mathbf{E}_{o\text{~not ~satisfy~}c}[R_{o}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{|\hat{A}^{\text{inter}}_{q,o,t}|}{|\hat{A}^{\text{DR.GRPO}}_{q,o,t}|}&gt;1,\text{ only when }|C^{+}_{q}|=|C^{-}_{q}|\text{ if }|C^{+}_{q}|\text{ is a constant. }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">inter</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">DR.GRPO</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> only when </mtext><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> is a constant.</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{|\hat{A}^{\text{inter}}_{q,o,t}|}{|\hat{A}^{\text{DR.GRPO}}_{q,o,t}|}&gt;1,\text{ only when }|C^{+}_{q}|=|C^{-}_{q}|\text{ if }|C^{+}_{q}|\text{ is a constant. }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.EGx6" title="Theorem 1 (Situations with clearer advantage signal (proved in Appendix )). ‣ 4.2 Advantage Estimation Based On Regrouping. ‣ 4 Conditional Advantage Estimation ‣ Conditional Advantage Estimation for Reinforcement Learning in Large Rea-soning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given a prompt <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, the set of all responses that satisfy condition <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> can be denoted as <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. We use <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\mathrm{P}(o\in\mathcal{C}|q,\theta)\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\mathrm{P}(o\in\mathcal{C}|q,\theta)\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> to describe the probability that a response <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying condition <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is provided to the prompt <math id="A4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> by an LLM with parameter <math id="A4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. Assuming that when condition <math id="A4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is satisfied, the probability of the correct response is <math id="A4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, and when condition <math id="A4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is not satisfied, the probability of the correct response is <math id="A4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{-}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denoting the correctness of the response <math id="A4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> to query <math id="A4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{o}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]=a_{+}\text{ and }\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]=a_{-}~." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]=a_{+}\text{ and }\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]=a_{-}~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>DR.GRPO</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sampling a group of responses <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> to the prompt <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, the advantage <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}^{\text{DR.GRPO}}_{q,o,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mtext>DR.GRPO</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{\text{DR.GRPO}}_{q,o,t}</annotation></semantics></math> of a response <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> can be calculated as:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{A}^{\text{DR.GRPO}}_{q,o,t}=R_{o}-\text{mean}(\{R_{o^{\prime}}|o^{\prime}\in G_{q}\})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mtext>DR.GRPO</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>mean</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{A}^{\text{DR.GRPO}}_{q,o,t}=R_{o}-\text{mean}(\{R_{o^{\prime}}|o^{\prime}\in G_{q}\}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We use <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\text{DR.GRPO}}(o,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mtext>DR.GRPO</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\text{DR.GRPO}}(o,c)</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the <span id="A4.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">average</span> advantage of the responses that <span id="A4.SS1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">satisfy</span> condition <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, and utilize <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{A}^{\text{DR.GRPO}}(o,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>DR.GRPO</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{A}^{\text{DR.GRPO}}(o,c)</annotation></semantics></math> to describe the average advantage of the other responses that <span id="A4.SS1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do not satisfy</span> condition <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A^{\text{DR.GRPO}}(o,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mtext>DR.GRPO</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A^{\text{DR.GRPO}}(o,c)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[\hat{A}^{\text{DR.GRPO}}_{q,o,t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mtext>DR.GRPO</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[\hat{A}^{\text{DR.GRPO}}_{q,o,t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]-\mathbf{E}_{o\in G_{q}}[R_{o}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]-\mathbf{E}_{o\in G_{q}}[R_{o}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a_{+}-[\mathrm{P}(o\in\mathcal{C}|q,\theta)\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]+\mathrm{P}(o\notin\mathcal{C}|q,\theta)\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a_{+}-[\mathrm{P}(o\in\mathcal{C}|q,\theta)\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]+\mathrm{P}(o\notin\mathcal{C}|q,\theta)\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a_{+}-pa_{+}-(1-p)a_{-}=(a_{+}-a_{-})(1-p)~," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a_{+}-pa_{+}-(1-p)a_{-}=(a_{+}-a_{-})(1-p)~,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{A}^{\text{DR.GRPO}}(o,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>DR.GRPO</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{A}^{\text{DR.GRPO}}(o,c)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(a_{-}-a_{+})p~." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(a_{-}-a_{+})p~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Inter-group Advantage (<span id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CANON-Inter</span>)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We sort the sampled responses based on the numerical value considered by condition <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, and split them at position <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> into two groups. Based on the symmetry of the inter-group advantage, we can denote these <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> responses as <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{+}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{+}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>. We use <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda:=\frac{|C_{q}^{+}|}{|G_{q}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda:=\frac{|C_{q}^{+}|}{|G_{q}|}</annotation></semantics></math> to simplify the notation, and denote the average inter-group advantage with <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\lambda}(o,c,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\lambda}(o,c,p)</annotation></semantics></math> for the responses that <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">satisfy</span> condition <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{A}_{\lambda}(o,c,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{A}_{\lambda}(o,c,p)</annotation></semantics></math> is utilized to represent the average inter-group advantage of those responses that <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do not satisfy</span> condition <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we can compute the average reward of each group as follows.</p>
<table id="A4.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{E}_{o\in C^{+}_{q}}[R_{o}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{E}_{o\in C^{+}_{q}}[R_{o}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[\mathrm{P}(o\in\mathcal{C}|q,\theta,o\in C^{+}_{q})\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]+\mathrm{P}(o\notin\mathcal{C}|q,\theta,o\in C^{+}_{q})\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[\mathrm{P}(o\in\mathcal{C}|q,\theta,o\in C^{+}_{q})\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]+\mathrm{P}(o\notin\mathcal{C}|q,\theta,o\in C^{+}_{q})\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.EGx13.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.EGx13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\frac{p}{\lambda}\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]+\frac{\lambda-p}{\lambda}\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}],\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}],\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\frac{p}{\lambda}\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]+\frac{\lambda-p}{\lambda}\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}],\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}],\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.EGx13.2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.EGx13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\frac{p}{\lambda}a_{+}+\frac{\lambda-p}{\lambda}a_{-},\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
a_{+},\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.~," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\frac{p}{\lambda}a_{+}+\frac{\lambda-p}{\lambda}a_{-},\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
a_{+},\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.~,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{E}_{o\notin C^{+}_{q}}[R_{o}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{E}_{o\notin C^{+}_{q}}[R_{o}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[\mathrm{P}(o\in\mathcal{C}|q,\theta,o\notin C^{+}_{q})\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]+\mathrm{P}(o\notin\mathcal{C}|q,\theta,o\notin C^{+}_{q})\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}R_{o}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[\mathrm{P}(o\in\mathcal{C}|q,\theta,o\notin C^{+}_{q})\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]+\mathrm{P}(o\notin\mathcal{C}|q,\theta,o\notin C^{+}_{q})\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}R_{o}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.EGx13.3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.EGx13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}],\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
\frac{p-\lambda}{1-\lambda}\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]+\frac{1-p}{1-\lambda}\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}],\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}],\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
\frac{p-\lambda}{1-\lambda}\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]+\frac{1-p}{1-\lambda}\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}],\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.EGx13.4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.EGx13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}a_{-},\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
\frac{p-\lambda}{1-\lambda}a_{+}+\frac{1-p}{1-\lambda}a_{-},\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.~." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}a_{-},\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
\frac{p-\lambda}{1-\lambda}a_{+}+\frac{1-p}{1-\lambda}a_{-},\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we can calculate the average advantages:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{\lambda}(o,c,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{\lambda}(o,c,p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}-\mathrm{P}(o\in C_{q}^{+}|q,\theta,o\in\mathcal{C})\mathbf{E}_{o^{\prime}\notin C^{+}_{q}}[R_{o^{\prime}}]-\mathrm{P}(o\notin C_{q}^{+}|q,\theta,o\in\mathcal{C})\mathbf{E}_{o^{\prime}\in C^{+}_{q}}[R_{o^{\prime}}]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}-\mathrm{P}(o\in C_{q}^{+}|q,\theta,o\in\mathcal{C})\mathbf{E}_{o^{\prime}\notin C^{+}_{q}}[R_{o^{\prime}}]-\mathrm{P}(o\notin C_{q}^{+}|q,\theta,o\in\mathcal{C})\mathbf{E}_{o^{\prime}\in C^{+}_{q}}[R_{o^{\prime}}]]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.EGx14.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.EGx14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]-\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}a_{-},\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
\frac{\lambda}{p}[\frac{p-\lambda}{1-\lambda}a_{+}+\frac{1-p}{1-\lambda}a_{-}],\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.-\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}0,\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
\frac{p-\lambda}{p}a_{+},\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{E}_{o\in\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]-\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}a_{-},\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
\frac{\lambda}{p}[\frac{p-\lambda}{1-\lambda}a_{+}+\frac{1-p}{1-\lambda}a_{-}],\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.-\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}0,\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
\frac{p-\lambda}{p}a_{+},\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.EGx14.2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.EGx14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}a_{+}-a_{-},\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
\frac{\lambda(1-p)}{p(1-\lambda)}(a_{+}-a_{-}),\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.~," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}a_{+}-a_{-},\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
\frac{\lambda(1-p)}{p(1-\lambda)}(a_{+}-a_{-}),\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.~,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{A}_{\lambda}(o,c,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{A}_{\lambda}(o,c,p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}-\mathrm{P}(o\in C_{q}^{+}|q,\theta,o\notin\mathcal{C})\mathbf{E}_{o^{\prime}\notin C^{+}_{q}}[R_{o^{\prime}}]-\mathrm{P}(o\notin C_{q}^{+}|q,\theta,o\notin\mathcal{C})\mathbf{E}_{o^{\prime}\in C^{+}_{q}}[R_{o^{\prime}}]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}-\mathrm{P}(o\in C_{q}^{+}|q,\theta,o\notin\mathcal{C})\mathbf{E}_{o^{\prime}\notin C^{+}_{q}}[R_{o^{\prime}}]-\mathrm{P}(o\notin C_{q}^{+}|q,\theta,o\notin\mathcal{C})\mathbf{E}_{o^{\prime}\in C^{+}_{q}}[R_{o^{\prime}}]]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.EGx15.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.EGx15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]-\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\frac{\lambda-p}{1-p}a_{-},\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
0,\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.-\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\frac{1-\lambda}{1-p}[\frac{p}{\lambda}a_{+}+\frac{\lambda-p}{\lambda}a_{-}],\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
a_{+},\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{E}_{o\notin\mathcal{C}}[R_{o}]-\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\frac{\lambda-p}{1-p}a_{-},\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
0,\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.-\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\frac{1-\lambda}{1-p}[\frac{p}{\lambda}a_{+}+\frac{\lambda-p}{\lambda}a_{-}],\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
a_{+},\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.EGx15.2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.EGx15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\frac{p(1-\lambda)}{\lambda(1-p)}(a_{-}-a_{+}),\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
a_{-}-a_{+},\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.~." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\frac{p(1-\lambda)}{\lambda(1-p)}(a_{-}-a_{+}),\text{if}~\lambda\geq p\\
\\
a_{-}-a_{+},\text{if}~\lambda&lt;p\\
\end{array}\right.~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Comparison</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have the ratio between inter-group advantage and DR.GRPO:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{|A_{\lambda}(o,c,p)|}{|A^{\text{DR.GRPO}}(o,c)|}=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{1-p}&gt;1&amp;\text{if }\lambda\geq p\\
\frac{\lambda}{(1-\lambda)p}&amp;\text{if }\lambda&lt;p\end{cases}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mtext>DR.GRPO</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{|A_{\lambda}(o,c,p)|}{|A^{\text{DR.GRPO}}(o,c)|}=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{1-p}&gt;1&amp;\text{if }\lambda\geq p\\
\frac{\lambda}{(1-\lambda)p}&amp;\text{if }\lambda&lt;p\end{cases},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{|\tilde{A}_{\lambda}(o,c,p)|}{|\tilde{A}^{\text{DR.GRPO}}(o,c)|}=\begin{cases}\frac{1-\lambda}{\lambda(1-p)}&amp;\text{if }\lambda\geq p\\
\frac{1}{p}&gt;1&amp;\text{if }\lambda&lt;p\end{cases}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>DR.GRPO</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{|\tilde{A}_{\lambda}(o,c,p)|}{|\tilde{A}^{\text{DR.GRPO}}(o,c)|}=\begin{cases}\frac{1-\lambda}{\lambda(1-p)}&amp;\text{if }\lambda\geq p\\
\frac{1}{p}&gt;1&amp;\text{if }\lambda&lt;p\end{cases}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">To accentuate the impact of a specific condition on advantages, the following is required:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1-\lambda}{\lambda(1-p)}&gt;1\text{ if }\lambda\geq p,\text{ and }\frac{\lambda}{(1-\lambda)p}&gt;1\text{ if }\lambda&lt;p." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1-\lambda}{\lambda(1-p)}&gt;1\text{ if }\lambda\geq p,\text{ and }\frac{\lambda}{(1-\lambda)p}&gt;1\text{ if }\lambda&lt;p.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Then we have</p>
<table id="A4.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda&lt;\frac{1}{2-p}\text{ if }\lambda\geq p,\text{ and }\lambda&gt;\frac{p}{1+p}\text{ if }\lambda&lt;p." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda&lt;\frac{1}{2-p}\text{ if }\lambda\geq p,\text{ and }\lambda&gt;\frac{p}{1+p}\text{ if }\lambda&lt;p.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C^{+}_{q}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C^{+}_{q}|</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant, <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is also a constant. Due to <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2-p}&gt;\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2-p}&gt;\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{p}{1+p}&lt;\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{p}{1+p}&lt;\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> needs to satisfy <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\leq\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\leq\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> at the same time, consequently restricting the value of <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> to 0.5. In this way, we have <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{|C^{+}_{q}|}{|C^{+}_{q}|+|C^{-}_{q}|}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{|C^{+}_{q}|}{|C^{+}_{q}|+|C^{-}_{q}|}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, and finally <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C^{+}_{q}|=|C^{-}_{q}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C^{+}_{q}|=|C^{-}_{q}|</annotation></semantics></math>
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
